-- title:
--   Left translation by an integral element fixes twisted orbital class terms
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields, $\sigma$ a $K$-automorphism of $L$ with every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lying in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and $D$ an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28) datum for $L/K$: a monoid homomorphism $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ into the continuous ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ restricting on $L$ to $\tau$. Fix a Haar measure $\nu_{Z_L}$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$, a finite set $S$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, a function $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,\infty})$ and a family $\varphi_S$ of functions on the groups $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ (the latter does not occur in the conclusion); a closed subgroup $H\le \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ whose members are exactly the $h$ with vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries such that $(D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma)(h)\,h^{-1}$, the entrywise image of $h$, times $h^{-1}$, is central; a Haar measure $\mu_H$ on $H$ that is in addition right-invariant; and a set $\Delta\subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ each of whose members $t$ has vanishing off-diagonal entries with $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11})\neq 1$, and such that for distinct $t,t'\in\Delta$ the sets $\{\delta : \exists g,\ t^{-1}g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g)\in Z(\mathrm{GL}_2(L))\}$ ($\sigma$ applied entrywise) are disjoint. The assertion is: for every finite set $T$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, every family $\psi$ of functions on the $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, every $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,f})$ such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (S ∪ T) φ φa φf ψ` holds — that is, $\varphi_a$ is a compactly supported smooth function of the archimedean matrix entries, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, each $\psi_v$ for $v\in S\cup T$ is locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f(h)=\prod_{v\in S\cup T}\psi_v(\mathrm{comp}_v h)$ whenever all semi-local components of $h$ outside $S\cup T$ are integral, $\varphi_f(h)=0$ if some component outside $S\cup T$ fails to be integral, and $\varphi(g)=\varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_f)$ — and such that $\psi_v$ is right-invariant under the integral set `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` for every $v\in T$: for every $g\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ with trivial archimedean part, with finite part in `finiteIntegralGL2` (both the matrix and its inverse integral), and with trivial semi-local component at every $v\notin T$, and for every $t\in\Delta$, the two class terms computed from $x\mapsto\varphi(g^{-1}x)$ coincide with those computed from $\varphi$. Here, for a test function $\phi$, the class term attaches to a class $q$ in the orbit quotient $H\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ the value $\int^{-}_{\mathbb{A}_L^\times}\|\phi\big(q_{\mathrm{out}}^{-1}\,\iota(t)\,(D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma)(z\cdot q_{\mathrm{out}})\big)\|\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)$, where $\iota(t)$ is the image of $t$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, $z$ is viewed as a central scalar matrix, $(D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma)$ acts entrywise, and $q_{\mathrm{out}}$ is the chosen representative; this is integrated over the quotient against the measure [`HaarQuotient.measure`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28) built from the adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, $H$ and $\mu_H$, first with no weight and secondly weighted by $\big|-\log \mathcal{H}(q_{\mathrm{out}})-\log \mathcal{H}(w\,q_{\mathrm{out}})\big|$, with $\mathcal{H}$ the adelic height (the product of the archimedean height of the infinite part and the finite height of the finite part) and $w$ the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ of the antidiagonal matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is the invariance, under left translation of the test function by an integral finite-adelic element concentrated at the marked places $T$, of the hyperbolic class terms (plain and height-weighted) that occur on the geometric side of the twisted trace formula for the cyclic extension $L/K$. It feeds the estimate [`AutomorphicForm.sum_lintegral_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_indicator_translate_mul_prod_measure_doubleCoset_le`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.sum_lintegral_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_indicator_translate_mul_prod_measure_doubleCoset_le), where these terms are summed over $t\in\Delta$ and compared with double-coset volumes.
